{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514476-maleficia-and-striga","id":1514476,"title":"Maleficia and Striga","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-10T10:14:18-07:00","id":1514476,"title":"Maleficia and Striga","content":"Good evening class!<br /> Tonight's topic will be some infernal goodies from the past!<br /> Topics and discussions about Dark Thaumaturgy and Infernalism bloomed lately, so I started to wonder... how many of my fellow Storyteller and players use/used the exotic disciplines, Maleficia and Striga?<br /> <br /> For the neonates, these two disciplines were in the 1997 <b>Dark Ages Companion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Striga</b> is an infernal Discipline associated with secret witch-cults in the Dark Ages of Europe. It encompasses hexes and dark connections to the natural world. It can only be used by Infernalist vampires. Practitioners are often referred to as strigmaga, or &quot;nightwalkers.&quot;\u200b<br /> \u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200bStrix: Call on the wind to bring the sound of distant conversations to the caster.<br /> <b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b Scobax: Summon swarms of insects and vermin the caster cannot control them beyond the summoning, they're merely incited to wreak havoc.<br /> <b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b <b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b Masca: Take on the form of a beast whose blood the user drank until the next sunrise.<br /> <b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b <b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200bHexe: Twist and mutate a target's body with a powerful curse.<br /> <b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b <b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b <b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b <b><b>\u2022</b></b>\u200b Fractura: Create barbed tentacles from the caster's own blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Maleficia</b> is a dark Discipline supposedly invented by infernalist Malkavians with the aid of demons in the Dark Ages of Europe. It encompasses a variety of curses to bring misery and misfortune upon others. It can only be used by infernalist vampires.<br /> \u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200bEvil Eye: Inflict a minor mishap on a target<br /> \u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200bMinor Curse: Inflict a series of mishaps on a target<br /> \u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200bPsalm of the Damned: Distract targets with a chant that follows them<br /> \u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200bBarren: Render the target unable to have children or Embrace<br /> \u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200b\u200b<b><b>\u2022 </b></b>\u200bGreater Curse: Inflict a hideous appearance and restless sleep on a target for a year\u200b<br /> <br /> So, in tandem with Dark Thaumaturgy and or Daimonion (or even just standalone disciplines) have you (ever) used them? Still suing them time to time?<br /> Or these two quietly faded from history? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T11:43:46-07:00","id":1514489,"title":"","content":"Never heard about &quot;Striga&quot; before. But I'm keeping an eye on this thread for more interesting information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T12:06:29-07:00","id":1514492,"title":"","content":"I've never used them in Vampire. But long ago I compiled most of the Dark Thaumaturgy and Infernalist Paths in a quick summary so I can use them for mortal infernalist covens, or combine them with certain types of fomori to boost them up for use in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> These two paths of Dark Thaumaturgy have a lot of classic horror feel or mirror classic witchcraft powers, so I can get good use out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:30:51-07:00","id":1514512,"title":"","content":"Nah. When I read the book I just thought they were the products of a time where what was a discipline or not wasn't so clear cut. By the methods of later editions These are clearly more thaumaturgy territory, not even the dark kind<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T15:25:04-07:00","id":1514517,"title":"","content":"I think i used both once in a chronicle as part of my own take on Koldunism - exactly because of the &quot;classic horror/witchcraft feel&quot; their powers seemed to mirror, as Black Fox described - but i overall glossed over the late 90s to early 00s period of WoD materials, my interest gravitating to other games and settings due to a number of factors at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-10-2023, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T04:04:28-07:00","id":1514565,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d completely missed these over the years, I\u2019d probably use them as Dark Thaumaturgy Paths rather than disciplines.<br /> <br /> I tend to use infernal or Wyrm investments and DT as the main sources of corrupt power for cultists or infernal possessed/formori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T07:11:22-07:00","id":1514575,"title":"","content":"I think at least <b>Maleficia</b>\u200b is kind of obsolete since you have several Blood Magic path that do something similar like the Path of Curses or the Evil Eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}